#: ../../source/references_shaders.md:1
msgid "Shader Pipeline & Composable Effects"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_shaders.md:3
msgid ""
"Post-processing effects applied to the pixel canvas (`numpy uint8 array, "
"shape (H,W,3)`) after character rendering and before encoding. Also "
"covers **pixel-level blend modes**, **feedback buffers**, and the "
"**ShaderChain** compositor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_shaders.md:5
msgid ""
"**See also:** composition.md (blend modes, tonemap) · effects.md · "
"scenes.md · architecture.md · optimization.md · troubleshooting.md"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_shaders.md:7
msgid ""
"**Blend modes:** For the 20 pixel blend modes and `blend_canvas()`, see "
"`composition.md`. All blending uses `blend_canvas(base, top, mode, "
"opacity)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_shaders.md:9
msgid "Design Philosophy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_shaders.md:11
msgid ""
"The shader pipeline turns raw ASCII renders into cinematic output. The "
"system is designed for **composability** — every shader, blend mode, and "
"feedback transform is an independent building block. Combining them "
"creates infinite visual variety from a small set of primitives."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_shaders.md:13
msgid "Choose shaders that reinforce the mood:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_shaders.md:14
msgid "**Retro terminal**: CRT + scanlines + grain + green/amber tint"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_shaders.md:15
msgid "**Clean modern**: light bloom + subtle vignette only"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_shaders.md:16
msgid ""
"**Glitch art**: heavy chromatic aberration + glitch bands + color wobble "
"+ pixel sort"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_shaders.md:17
msgid "**Cinematic**: bloom + vignette + grain + color grade"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_shaders.md:18
msgid "**Dreamy**: heavy bloom + soft focus + color wobble + low contrast"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_shaders.md:19
msgid "**Harsh/industrial**: high contrast + grain + scanlines + no bloom"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_shaders.md:20
msgid ""
"**Psychedelic**: color wobble + chromatic + kaleidoscope mirror + high "
"saturation + feedback with hue shift"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_shaders.md:21
msgid "**Data corruption**: pixel sort + data bend + block glitch + posterize"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_shaders.md:22
msgid ""
"**Recursive/infinite**: feedback buffer with zoom + screen blend + hue "
"shift"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_shaders.md:26
msgid "Pixel-Level Blend Modes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_shaders.md:28
msgid ""
"All operate on float32 [0,1] canvases for precision. Use "
"`blend_canvas(base, top, mode, opacity)` which handles uint8 <-> float "
"conversion."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_shaders.md:30
msgid "Available Modes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_shaders.md:57
msgid "Usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_shaders.md:75
msgid "Creative Combinations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_shaders.md:77
msgid ""
"**Feedback + difference** = psychedelic color evolution (each frame XORs "
"with the previous)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_shaders.md:78
msgid "**Screen + screen** = additive glow stacking"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_shaders.md:79
msgid ""
"**Multiply** on two different effects = only shows where both have "
"brightness (intersection)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_shaders.md:80
msgid ""
"**Exclusion** between two layers = creates complementary patterns where "
"they differ"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_shaders.md:81
msgid "**Color dodge/burn** = extreme contrast enhancement at overlap zones"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_shaders.md:82
msgid ""
"**Hard mix** = reduces everything to pure black/white/color at "
"intersections"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_shaders.md:86
msgid "Feedback Buffer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_shaders.md:88
msgid ""
"Recursive temporal effect: frame N-1 feeds back into frame N with decay "
"and optional spatial transform. Creates trails, echoes, smearing, zoom "
"tunnels, rotation feedback, rainbow trails."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_shaders.md:111
msgid "Feedback Presets"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_shaders.md:143
msgid "ShaderChain"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_shaders.md:145
msgid ""
"Composable shader pipeline. Build chains of named shaders with "
"parameters. Order matters — shaders are applied sequentially to the "
"canvas."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_shaders.md:174
msgid "`_apply_shader_step()` — Full Dispatch Function"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_shaders.md:176
msgid ""
"Routes shader names to implementations. Some shaders have **audio-"
"reactive scaling** — the dispatch function reads `f[\"bdecay\"]` and "
"`f[\"rms\"]` to modulate parameters on the beat."
msgstr ""

